Chapter 10: "The Lion King's Country"

Chapter 10.30: "Ballpoint Pen"

After changing not just the wig and makeup, but also the dress, Subaru returned to the main hall of the hunting lodge having erased all traces of the operation. The others were just beginning to gather as well.

The hunting lodge was what one might call a cabin, far more spacious than its name suggested, with an environment capable of accommodating multiple people staying overnight. That said, with all the key members who had participated in the operation at the Morrow estate gathered in one place, it was understandably cramped.

So when Subaru spotted an unusual face among them, he raised an eyebrow with an "Oh."

"'Black Dog' being here is rare. You usually don't join these discussions, do you?"

"Kuhahaha, it's not like I'm eager or leaning forward about it. I'm just being nagged—loudly and repeatedly—to attend the strategy meetings from now on. That's the pain of serving at court, I suppose."

The one laughing with a cackle while leaning against the wall at the edge of the hall, legs sprawled out on the floor, was 'Black Dog.' Like Subaru, who had changed out of his dress, he too had shed his serving attire and was back in his usual mask and robe.

Personally, Subaru thought he was a handsome man with no need to hide his face, but perhaps everyone had their own way of seeing things.

"Anyway, hearing a normally slacking guy talk about the pains of court service doesn't really resonate. If you don't get your act together, the burden on 'White Sheep' is gonna be insane, you know."

"Oi oi, give it a rest with that fickle, indiscriminate attitude of yours. Half-elf, duke, and now the little one—how many do you need to surround yourself with before you're satisfied, pretty boy?"

"Even if Subaru being fickle is true, your attitude is beyond intolerable. In Betty's eyes, 'White Sheep' is simply pitiable. Perhaps I should reward her by massaging her shoulders sometime."

"I think that's a good idea. Beako's shoulder massages aren't effective at all, but they're cute and soothing."

Responding to 'Black Dog,' who made a throat-slitting gesture with his thumb while delivering his sarcasm, Subaru and Beatrice both responded with thumbs-down boos.

The finger gestures themselves were rather menacing, but this was the amicable communication they'd cultivated over the past two months. Subaru had taught it to him, and surprisingly, 'Black Dog' seemed to have taken a liking to it.

"'Ash Star' and 'Librarian,' I apologize on behalf of 'Black Dog.' I believe he does have... ill intent, but no malice. Probably. Truly."

Apologizing for 'Black Dog's' attitude was his guardian figure, 'White Sheep.'

As she offered tea cups held in both hands, Subaru replied with an awkward smile, "No, no," and gratefully accepted cups for himself and Beatrice.

"'White Sheep' isn't the one who should be apologizing. He's a grown adult, so let him wipe his own ass. ...Oh, this is good. As expected, you know my preferences."

"Thank you for your concern! Also, the tea's flavor wasn't my doing—it was 'Blue Snake' who helped and matched it to your taste."

"Hm, Feri... 'Blue Snake' did?"

Barely managing to stop himself from using her name, Subaru looked toward the center of the room.

There, at a simple small table, Crusch—who had played a major role in the earlier operation—sat with her arms crossed and eyes closed, resting her body. When a cup was placed before her, the eye not covered by the eyepatch opened, meeting the gaze of Ferris, who had set the cup down.

Ferris, who had probably wanted to place it there unnoticed, sighed with resignation and—

"...Tea, Lady 'Verdant Splendor.'"

"Ah, my thanks."

"How is your body?"

"I cannot say I'm in peak condition, but compared to before, I'm no longer being thrown around by the power. I'll just have to manage by tricking it along."

"I see. The tea's been made lukewarm."

"Is that so. I struggle with hot things, so that helps."

"I know."

"I see."

With a nod of acknowledgment, Crusch brought the tea to her lips, and Ferris took a seat on the opposite side of the table—the farthest from her—and propped his chin on his hand. —Despite being such a casual exchange, the tension was at maximum.

"I-I nearly forgot to breathe there..."

"Actually, Subaru, you were holding your breath. Betty nearly suffocated along with you. Can't something be done about that?"

"I've been wanting to do something about it for these past two months, but..."

The situation was full of worries, but the most immediate concern was the friction between Crusch and Ferris, as just demonstrated.

Subaru only knew the barest details of how things had come to this, and he continued fumbling anxiously, uncertain how much a third party could help repair the rift in their master-servant relationship. —What was needed was the kind of role Otto had played in the "Sanctuary," reconciling Subaru and Emilia.

"Since he's not here, I can honestly praise him—that guy's amazing sometimes. How does he come up with a vision for restoring such a tangled relationship to normal?"

"Would it not work to lock those two in a box together, like with Subaru and Emilia?"

"If we put those two in a box now, it'd probably just be awkward silence..."

In the first place, Subaru and Emilia hadn't simply been put in a box and made up.

Of course, Subaru had made his own efforts to encourage the restoration of Crusch and Ferris's relationship—trying to bring up topics with both simultaneously, attempting to create time for just the two of them. But those efforts had continued to misfire, either becoming communication mediated through Subaru wedged between them, or proving unnecessary due to their still-perfect coordination that required no words.

For this operation too, he had initially proposed having Ferris play the wife role instead of Subaru, but—

"She absolutely refused, declaring she would never wear a dress."

"Yeah. Damn, if Natsumi hadn't been around, what would've happened to the operation? Putting Latchins aside, 'Black Dog' could never wear a dress."

"...It's not necessarily a rule that someone absolutely had to crossdress, you know."

"But thanks to that, we caught the fake viscount off guard, and Beako could hide inside the pannier. It was effective not just two or three ways—a proven track record from the Empire. No reason not to do it. —Q.E.D."

"Betty feels like she was just forcibly persuaded by some dubious logic...?"

Pouting and making the face of a girl at a troubled age, Beatrice had her head patted by Subaru. Just then, arriving a bit late, Russell and the others came in, apparently having been talking in another room.

"Apologies for interrupting your pleasant conversation. Let's discuss our future course of action."

Speaking, Russell accepted a tea cup from 'White Sheep.' Behind him, Latchins followed with a weary expression, and Subaru nudged him in the side with an elbow. "Hey."

"What were you talking about? Plotting more mischief together?"

"Together, my ass! Are your eyes just for show? I got nothing but tedious busywork shoved onto me. That bastard must be mistaking me for a slave or something."

"Well, if we're talking about holding the power of life and death over someone, then me, you, and Beako could all be called Russell's slaves."

"If that's the case, then the burden's way too lopsided toward me! You bastards could at least— ...Ah, never mind. Leaving things to you lot would be way more anxiety-inducing."

"That's probably exactly it, you know."

"Huh?" Latchins replied, seemingly unaware of his own long-suffering nature. But that disposition was undoubtedly why Russell had such high expectations of him.

His manner of speaking was rough, but he was probably actually the diligent civil servant type. He hadn't heard the details, but perhaps the surprising background of being from a distinguished family played a role too.

At any rate—

"—We've received word from 'Pink Rabbit.' It seems we can expect progress against the 'Beloved Children.'"

At Russell's report, delivered with his hand on the small table, the atmosphere immediately grew tense.

Naturally, Subaru took his seat with Beatrice on his lap, and Russell watched with satisfaction as everyone except 'Black Dog'—who sat on the floor—gathered around the table.

"Through our recent cooperation, 'Verdant Splendor' and the others should fully understand the danger of the 'Beloved Children.' Unless they are fundamentally eliminated, the Kingdom's collapse is unavoidable."

"Yeah, it's not just about tonight. With these 'Replacement Dolls' popping up all over the place, you can't even safely hug anyone."

"For Betty, that's a matter of life and death."

Nodding in agreement with Beatrice in her usual spot on his lap, Subaru bit the inside of his cheek thinking about the reach of the 'Beloved Children' plaguing the Kingdom—its penetration far exceeding imagination.

Unless this problem was resolved, even if Emilia could be crowned, she couldn't possibly build the country she desired. This was a dark cloud that Subaru had to dispel—as one living in this Kingdom, and above all, as the knight of a Royal Selection candidate.

"So, 'Pink Rabbit,' was it? What did she have to say? That she got her hands on a list of 'Beloved Children,' or found their base?"

"I understand your expectations, but a list likely doesn't exist. Only their mother holds all the information... Not sharing information and isolating them was part of her discipline, wasn't it?"

"Um, yes. She was that kind of person."

Touched by memories that must have been painful to recall, 'White Sheep' lowered her eyebrows slightly.

The flow continued to direct more hatred toward the leader of the 'Beloved Children'—Capella of 'Lust.' Ferris's expectations weren't far from Subaru's own. If there was progress in the fight against the 'Beloved Children,' they wanted to seize any chance to wipe them all out at once.

"But if that's not it, then what information did you get?"

"—Information that it might be possible to restore those affected by the authority of 'Lust,' including the 'Replacement Dolls,' back to normal."

"—!"

In that instant, the one who made their chair screech as they stood was Ferris.

Leaning on the small table, his eyes widened and his lips trembled.

"Back to normal... you mean they can be cured? All those people?"

"It's merely a possibility—a lead, nothing more. Calm yourself, 'Blue Snake.'"

"How can I be calm! Because, if such a thing exists..."

Trailing off mid-sentence, Ferris lowered his head, and Subaru could guess the continuation.

Probably, it went like this: —If such a method existed, they wouldn't have relied on the 'Dragon God Church.' And if they hadn't relied on the 'Dragon God Church,' Crusch would still be—

But—

"No matter how much you regret the past, all you gain is helplessness. Reflection is fine, but I cannot imagine that clinging to it will yield good results."

Ferris's remorse was denied by none other than Crusch herself.

As Ferris's cheek stiffened painfully, Subaru looked toward Crusch. But with even her uncovered eye closed, Crusch offered no answer he could grasp.

"As I just said, the information we've obtained is a lead toward resolution... At minimum, it should contribute to clarifying the principles behind 'Lust's' authority. Once we understand that, we can find countermeasures."

"Currently, while my 'Wind Reading' Divine Protection can verify truth from falsehood, it cannot save the victims of that authority. Looking at my own circumstances, there are certain methods, but—"

"—Our honest position is that we want to avoid relying on the 'Dragon God Church's' sacraments as much as possible."

At Russell's quiet but firm tone that brooked no argument, Subaru couldn't help but be taken aback.

"I'm glad you're being honest, but why is that? I mean, the sacraments actually do have an effect... well, you know."

"My own body is proof of their effectiveness. —The sacrament of Filore healed me. Of course, whether 'Lust's' authority and what ate away at my body can be treated as the same is unclear."

Taking over from the hesitant Subaru, Crusch—the person in question—spoke herself.

In response to that question, Russell touched his beard and cast a glance toward 'White Sheep.' Receiving it, 'White Sheep' gave a small nod and—

"I know about Filore. Whether or not that girl is suited to be a Royal Selection candidate aside, the 'Dragon God Church' is certainly not an organization that can be fully trusted. ...I too was a member of the Church during my time as a 'Beloved Child.' There are surely others—"

"The 'Beloved Children' have even infiltrated the Church... though that's hardly surprising given that the bigwigs at the castle had already been taken out. And..."

"—Tiga Lauleon. That one seemed to have sided with the enemy as well."

At Subaru's brief glance, Crusch nodded and brought up Tiga's name.

Tiga was the one who had fought Crusch at Miklotov's estate and had apparently reported Subaru—who had fled with Crusch afterward—as an accomplice in Miklotov's assassination. Judging from the circumstances, the likelihood that he was cooperating with the 'Beloved Children' faction was quite high. —There was even the possibility that he himself was one of the 'Beloved Children.'

"I thought we could've become friends... but no point regretting it. Anyway, so the 'Dragon God Church' isn't unified, and the 'Beloved Children' have definitely infiltrated it. So we can't carelessly rely on the sacraments—is that it?"

"————"

"Huh? 'White Sheep'?"

"Ah, I'm sorry, I was spacing out!"

At Subaru's repeated call, 'White Sheep' hurriedly answered.

Though rather than just spacing out, Subaru was concerned by how her demeanor seemed like she was enduring pain, or thinking of something far away.

However, before Subaru could press the matter, Russell cleared his throat, interrupting—

"Even setting that aside, I believe it is healthy to maintain a certain distance from the Royal Castle and the 'Dragon God Church.' Regardless of the new Royal Selection candidate's intentions, I don't want to take steps that would make the 'Dragon God Church's' influence grow too large."

"Hah, do we really have the luxury to pick and choose our moves in this situation? If the country falls while you're being picky, that'd be a fine additional disgrace for the 'Six-Tongued.'"

"Of course, I have no intention of misjudging priorities. If we have no other options, we'll have no choice but to rely on the 'Dragon God Church's' sacraments. Though even that isn't a realistic proposal unless we can identify the enemy within the 'Dragon God Church.'"

"—So with all this and that and everything? Why don't you let us hear this supposedly realistic and feasible plan of yours?"

Interjecting as Russell took over the explanation from 'White Sheep' was 'Black Dog.' Still sprawled on the floor with his long legs stretched out, 'Black Dog' laughed at the gathered gazes—"What, something wrong?"—

"I've just run out of patience with this conversation that won't move forward or continue. Now, speak up, lay it all out! Otherwise... I'm reaching the limit of both my sleepiness and my patience!"

"—. As I've said, if we can understand the principles behind 'Lust's' authority, we might be able to establish a path to countermeasures without the sacraments. However, that requires certain knowledge."

"Certain knowledge?"

"Yes. And that's where I need to consult you, 'Ash Star.'"

Though not entirely satisfied with being prompted by 'Black Dog,' Russell's words as he advanced the discussion made Subaru point at himself and tilt his head.

What on earth could Russell need to consult Subaru about at this point in the conversation?

"I'll help with anything I can, but consult me about what?"

"—I want to contact Roswaal. I'd like to rely on his knowledge. So, do you have any idea how to get in touch with him, given that he's gone into hiding?"

"Contact Roswaal?"

Hearing that name, Beatrice furrowed her brow suspiciously.

Like Emilia and the others confined at the castle, and Rem and the others who had fled the Royal Capital, Roswaal had also disappeared along with Frederica, Ryuzu and her replica sisters the 'Meyers' who had been at the Roswaal estate, and Sylphie.

From what Subaru had heard, Roswaal had refused the summons to the Royal Castle and given them the slip, which put him squarely on the wanted list. —In other words, the entire faction were wanted fugitives.

"But we don't know the whereabouts of anyone except Emilia and Ram, who are at the castle. Roswaal is no exception. You know that too, right, Russell... 'Silver Fox'?"

"Yes, that's what I was told. At least, according to what was reported to me."

"—. So, in other words, you suspect that Betty and the others have some means of contacting Roswaal and the others that we've been keeping secret from you?"

"Even if you did, it would be perfectly natural caution and preparation, so I won't fault you for it."

"You yourself, if you were truly friends, wouldn't be surprising to have one or two methods of contact."

"Unfortunately, it seems those three or four have all been eliminated. Originally, I couldn't even place any of the 'Six-Tongued' around Roswaal, so he's genuinely missing."

Beatrice's gaze at the shrugging Russell was stern.

But from Subaru's perspective, this was a fruitless quarrel. After all, Subaru's group had no means of contacting Roswaal either—Russell's suspicious nature was just a bad habit of his. Possibly an occupational hazard.

"By the way, what's this about wanting to borrow Roswaal's knowledge?"

Depending on the answer, they might find what they needed without relying on Roswaal.

Of course, Russell's side had probably thoroughly considered it and concluded Roswaal was the one, but asking was free.

When Subaru asked with that thought in mind, Russell narrowed his eyes slightly and—

"—Regarding research on the 'Witches.'"

"Eh..."

Hearing the word that emerged, Subaru's eyes widened and he held his breath.

Ignoring Subaru's reaction, Russell nodded and—

"It seems one of the 'Witches' was researching the transmutation of souls, and I want to look into that knowledge. —Though, if you know someone else who fits that description, they need not necessarily be Roswaal."

　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　△▼△▼△▼△

—Research on 'Witches' could serve as a counter to 'Lust's' authority.

"That was a blind spot. Actually, since we're talking about the Witch Cult, it's strange that the word 'Witch' itself came as a surprise. Those guys barely ever talk about the 'Witches.'"

By some twist of fate, Subaru had encountered all the Sin Archbishops except 'Pride'—apparently there were six positions—but the only one who properly went on about 'Witches' was Petelgeuse. He didn't recall any of the others mentioning the 'Witches.'

"No, Sirius said something too, I think. But that also felt like bitter grumbling about Petelgeuse being taken from her..."

"Either way, it's nothing good. The thought of those people talking about the 'Witches'—about Mother—makes my skin crawl just thinking about it."

Responding to Subaru's muttering, Beatrice's tone was weak and her demeanor distracted. Subaru sat down beside her on the bed, pulled her head close, and held her against his chest.

They had wrapped up the discussion in the main hall and retreated to one of the rooms in the hunting lodge. Luxuriously, it was a room just for Subaru and Beatrice, so they could open up freely here.

"It's not like I've been keeping secrets even when everyone's around."

Unfortunately, that attitude didn't seem to be understood—at least not by Russell.

